### Check for existing issues - [X] I have searched the existing issues and checked that my issue is not a duplicate. ### What happened? `POST /v1/batches` with a body missing `input_file_id`, `endpoint` or `completion_window` returns HTTP 500 with a Python `TypeError` message. OpenAI returns HTTP 400 for the same requests: ```json { "error": { "message": "Missing required parameter: 'input_file_id'.", "type": "invalid_request_error", "param": "input_file_id", "code": "missing_required_parameter" } } ``` ### Code as it stands at v1.94.3 `litellm/types/llms/openai.py:428` and `:443`: ```python class CreateBatchRequest(TypedDict, total=False): completion_window: Literal["24h"] endpoint: Literal["/v1/chat/completions", "/v1/embeddings", "/v1/completions"] input_file_id: str metadata: Optional[Dict[str, str]] output_expires_after: FileExpiresAfter extra_headers: Optional[Dict[str, str]] extra_body: Optional[Dict[str, str]] timeout: Optional[float] class LiteLLMBatchCreateRequest(CreateBatchRequest, total=False): model: str ``` `litellm/proxy/batches_endpoints/endpoints.py:126`, inside `create_batch`: ```python _create_batch_data = LiteLLMBatchCreateRequest(**data) ``` `litellm/batches/main.py:104`: ```python async def acreate_batch( completion_window: Literal["24h"], endpoint: Literal["/v1/chat/completions", "/v1/embeddings", "/v1/completions"], input_file_id: str, custom_llm_provider: Literal["openai", "azure", "vertex_ai", "bedrock", "hosted_vllm"] = "openai", metadata: Optional[Dict[str, str]] = None, ... ``` No request-body validation runs between the handler and `acreate_batch`. --- ### User Flow **Before a (hypothetical) fix: a developer submitting a nightly bulk classification job omits one field and receives a 500** 1. They send `POST https://litellm-domain/v1/files` with `purpose=batch` and their JSONL, and receive a file ID 2. They send `POST https://litellm-domain/v1/batches` with `{"endpoint": "/v1/chat/completions", "completion_window": "24h"}`, omitting `input_file_id` 3. The response is `500` with the message `acreate_batch() missing 1 required positional argument: 'input_file_id'` and `"type": "internal_server_error"` 4. Their SDK, which retries on 5xx, resends the same request and receives the same 500 each time **After a (hypothetical) fix: the same request returns 400 naming the absent field** 1. They send `POST https://litellm-domain/v1/files` with `purpose=batch` and their JSONL, and receive a file ID 2. They send `POST https://litellm-domain/v1/batches` with `{"endpoint": "/v1/chat/completions", "completion_window": "24h"}`, omitting `input_file_id` 3. The response is `400` with `"Missing required parameter: 'input_file_id'."`, `"param": "input_file_id"` and `"code": "missing_required_parameter"` 4. Their SDK does not retry a 4xx --- ### Proof the bug occurs **Version**: `litellm 1.94.3`, image digest `sha256:b7d979bac2a9e8fbb7d55272ef5f1f4a08ab365de8f78b1800834ca718d4c941`. No provider call is made on this path. **Config the proxy ran with** ```yaml model_list: - model_name: gpt-5-batch litellm_params: model: azure/gpt-5-batch-2025-08-07 api_base: os.environ/AZURE_API_BASE api_key: os.environ/AZURE_API_KEY general_settings: master_key: os.environ/LITELLM_MASTER_KEY database_url: os.environ/DATABASE_URL ``` **Commands and their full output** ``` $ for body in '{"endpoint": "/v1/chat/completions", "completion_window": "24h"}' \ '{"input_file_id": "file-abc", "completion_window": "24h"}' \ '{"input_file_id": "file-abc", "endpoint": "/v1/chat/completions"}' \ '{}'; do echo "--- body: $body" curl -s -w '
HTTP %{http_code}
' http://localhost:4000/v1/batches \ -H "Authorization: Bearer $LITELLM_KEY" \ -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d "$body" done --- body: {"endpoint": "/v1/chat/completions", "completion_window": "24h"} {"error":{"message":"acreate_batch() missing 1 required positional argument: 'input_file_id'","type":"internal_server_error","param":"None","code":"500"}} HTTP 500 --- body: {"input_file_id": "file-abc", "completion_window": "24h"} {"error":{"message":"acreate_batch() missing 1 required positional argument: 'endpoint'","type":"internal_server_error","param":"None","code":"500"}} HTTP 500 --- body: {"input_file_id": "file-abc", "endpoint": "/v1/chat/completions"} {"error":{"message":"acreate_batch() missing 1 required positional argument: 'completion_window'","type":"internal_server_error","param":"None","code":"500"}} HTTP 500 --- body: {} {"error":{"message":"acreate_batch() missing 3 required positional arguments: 'completion_window', 'endpoint', and 'input_file_id'","type":"internal_server_error","param":"None","code":"500"}} HTTP 500 ``` Same endpoint with all three fields present, against a real uploaded file: ``` $ curl -s -w '
HTTP %{http_code}
' http://localhost:4000/v1/batches \ -H "Authorization: Bearer $LITELLM_KEY" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \ -d "{"input_file_id":"$FILE_ID","endpoint":"/v1/chat/completions","completion_window":"24h"}" {"id":"bGl0ZWxsbV9wcm94eTttb2RlbF9pZDo0ZDhhNWVmMGY2Y2M5OTZkMmEwYzlmYmEzYTMxMzQ5Mjg0OTYxNWNhM2E2YmJjNGRjOTcyMDQ0Mjg4MTBmMjk0O2xsbV9iYXRjaF9pZDpiYXRjaF8yMDI2MDgxNy0wNTU3LjAxOQ","completion_window":"24h", ...} HTTP 200 ``` ### What part of LiteLLM is this about? Proxy ### What LiteLLM version are you on ? v1.94.3

### Check for existing issues - [X] I have searched the existing issues and checked that my issue is not a duplicate. ### What happened? On `POST /v1/batches`: - `"metadata": "abc"` returns HTTP 200. The batch is created and the returned object has `metadata: null`. A retrieve of that batch also reports `metadata: null`. - `"litellm_metadata": "abc"` returns HTTP 500 with the message `'str' object has no attribute 'update'`. OpenAI returns HTTP 400 for both: ```json { "error": { "message": "Invalid type for 'metadata': expected an object, but got a string instead.", "type": "invalid_request_error", "param": "metadata", "code": "invalid_type" } } ``` A list or a number in either field produces the same two outcomes. ### Code as it stands at v1.94.3 `litellm/proxy/litellm_pre_call_utils.py:1477`, `metadata`: ```python if "metadata" in data and data["metadata"] is not None: if isinstance(data["metadata"], str): data["metadata"] = safe_json_loads(data["metadata"]) if not isinstance(data["metadata"], dict): verbose_proxy_logger.warning( f"Failed to parse 'metadata' as JSON dict. Received value: {data['metadata']}" ) ``` `safe_json_loads` returns its `default` of `None` for unparseable input. `litellm/proxy/litellm_pre_call_utils.py:1491`, `litellm_metadata`: ```python if "litellm_metadata" in data and data["litellm_metadata"] is not None: if isinstance(data["litellm_metadata"], str): parsed_litellm_metadata = safe_json_loads(data["litellm_metadata"]) if not isinstance(parsed_litellm_metadata, dict): verbose_proxy_logger.warning(...) else: data["litellm_metadata"] = parsed_litellm_metadata ``` `litellm/proxy/litellm_pre_call_utils.py:1033`: ```python data[_metadata_variable_name].update(user_api_key_logged_metadata) ``` `_metadata_variable_name` is returned by `_get_metadata_variable_name` (`:372`), which reads `LITELLM_METADATA_ROUTES` (`:114`): ```python LITELLM_METADATA_ROUTES = ( "batches", "bedrock", "/v1/messages", "responses", "files", ) ``` --- ### User Flow **Before a (hypothetical) fix: a team tagging each batch with a cost centre receives 200 and the tag is absent from the batch** 1. They send `POST https://litellm-domain/v1/files` with `purpose=batch` and their JSONL, and receive a file ID 2. Their client serialises metadata to a JSON string, so they send `POST https://litellm-domain/v1/batches` with `"metadata": "{"cost_centre": "research"}"` 3. The response is `200` carrying a batch ID, and `"metadata": null` 4. They send `GET https://litellm-domain/v1/batches/{batch_id}` and the response reports `"metadata": null` and `"status": "completed"` 5. A colleague sends the same request naming the field `litellm_metadata` instead, and receives `500` with `'str' object has no attribute 'update'` **After a (hypothetical) fix: both requests return 400 identifying the field and its type** 1. They send `POST https://litellm-domain/v1/files` with `purpose=batch` and their JSONL, and receive a file ID 2. They send `POST https://litellm-domain/v1/batches` with `"metadata": "{"cost_centre": "research"}"` 3. The response is `400` with `"Invalid type for 'metadata': expected an object, but got a string instead."` and `"param": "metadata"` 4. They resend with `"metadata": {"cost_centre": "research"}` and receive `200`; `GET https://litellm-domain/v1/batches/{batch_id}` reports `"metadata": {"cost_centre": "research"}` 5. The colleague using `litellm_metadata` receives `400` rather than `500` --- ### Proof the bug occurs **Version**: `litellm 1.94.3`, image digest `sha256:b7d979bac2a9e8fbb7d55272ef5f1f4a08ab365de8f78b1800834ca718d4c941` **Config the proxy ran with** ```yaml model_list: - model_name: gpt-5-batch litellm_params: model: azure/gpt-5-batch-2025-08-07 api_base: os.environ/AZURE_API_BASE api_key: os.environ/AZURE_API_KEY general_settings: master_key: os.environ/LITELLM_MASTER_KEY database_url: os.environ/DATABASE_URL ``` **Commands and their full output** Upload a batch input file: ``` $ printf '%s
' '{"custom_id":"1","method":"POST","url":"/v1/chat/completions","body":{"model":"gpt-5-batch","messages":[{"role":"user","content":"hi"}]}}' > batch_input.jsonl $ FILE_ID=$(curl -s http://localhost:4000/v1/files -H "Authorization: Bearer $LITELLM_KEY" \ -F purpose=batch -F 'target_model_names=gpt-5-batch' -F file=@batch_input.jsonl \ | python3 -c 'import json,sys; print(json.load(sys.stdin)["id"])') ``` `metadata` as an object: ``` $ curl -s -w '
HTTP %{http_code}
' http://localhost:4000/v1/batches \ -H "Authorization: Bearer $LITELLM_KEY" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \ -d "{"input_file_id":"$FILE_ID","endpoint":"/v1/chat/completions","completion_window":"24h","metadata":{"cost_centre":"research"}}" {"id":"bGl0ZWxsbV9wcm94eTttb2RlbF9pZDo0ZDhhNWVmMGY2Y2M5OTZkMmEwYzlmYmEzYTMxMzQ5Mjg0OTYxNWNhM2E2YmJjNGRjOTcyMDQ0Mjg4MTBmMjk0O2xsbV9iYXRjaF9pZDpiYXRjaF8yMDI2MDgxNy0wNTU3LjAxOQ","completion_window":"24h", ...} HTTP 200 ``` `metadata` as a string: ``` $ curl -s -w '
HTTP %{http_code}
' http://localhost:4000/v1/batches \ -H "Authorization: Bearer $LITELLM_KEY" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \ -d "{"input_file_id":"$FILE_ID","endpoint":"/v1/chat/completions","completion_window":"24h","metadata":"abc"}" HTTP 200 metadata = None ``` Retrieve of that batch: ``` $ curl -s "http://localhost:4000/v1/batches/$BATCH_ID" -H "Authorization: Bearer $LITELLM_KEY" \ | python3 -c 'import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(" retrieved metadata =", repr(d.get("metadata")), "| status:", d.get("status"))' retrieved metadata = None | status: completed ``` `litellm_metadata` as a string: ``` $ curl -s -w '
HTTP %{http_code}
' http://localhost:4000/v1/batches \ -H "Authorization: Bearer $LITELLM_KEY" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \ -d "{"input_file_id":"$FILE_ID","endpoint":"/v1/chat/completions","completion_window":"24h","litellm_metadata":"abc"}" {"error":{"message":"'str' object has no attribute 'update'","type":"internal_server_error","param":"None","code":"500"}} HTTP 500 ``` The three requests differ only in the metadata field's name and type. ### What part of LiteLLM is this about? Proxy ### What LiteLLM version are you on ? v1.94.3

### Check for existing issues - [X] I have searched the existing issues and checked that my issue is not a duplicate. ### What happened? On a proxy with no `OPENAI_API_KEY` and no `OPENAI_API_BASE` in its environment, whose deployments carry their own credentials: | Request | Observed | OpenAI returns | | --- | --- | --- | | `GET /v1/batches/{unknown_id}` | 500 `The api_key client option must be set either by passing api_key to the client or by setting the OPENAI_API_KEY environment variable` | 404 `batch_not_found` | | `POST /v1/batches/{unknown_id}/cancel` | same 500 | 404 `batch_not_found` | | `POST /v1/batches` with an unresolvable `input_file_id` | same 500 | 404 `No such File object` | ### Code as it stands at v1.94.3 `litellm/proxy/batches_endpoints/endpoints.py` contains four such fallbacks, one per handler: | Handler | Line | | --- | --- | | `create_batch` | `:124` | | `retrieve_batch` | `:495` | | `list_batches` | `:688` | | `cancel_batch` | `:875` | `retrieve_batch` at `:489`: ```python # SCENARIO 3: Fallback to custom_llm_provider (uses env variables) else: custom_llm_provider = ( provider or get_custom_llm_provider_from_request_headers(request=request) or get_custom_llm_provider_from_request_query(request=request) or "openai" ) response = await litellm.aretrieve_batch(...) ``` Branch selection into this block is a function of the id string: `decode_model_from_file_id` and `_is_base64_encoded_unified_file_id` both read only the id, and `get_batch_from_database()` returns `(None, None)` unless the id is a unified id. An id that names a provider through a path param, body key, header or `?custom_llm_provider` does not reach this block. --- ### User Flow **Before a (hypothetical) fix: an engineer checking a batch id from an old job log receives a message about a missing API key** 1. Their job log records a batch id, so they send `GET https://litellm-domain/v1/batches/batch_68a1f2c9deadbeef` 2. The batch was purged and the id resolves to nothing 3. The response is `500` with `The api_key client option must be set either by passing api_key to the client or by setting the OPENAI_API_KEY environment variable` and `"type": "internal_server_error"` 4. They send `POST https://litellm-domain/v1/batches/batch_68a1f2c9deadbeef/cancel` and receive the identical `500` and message 5. They submit a new batch with a mistyped `input_file_id` via `POST https://litellm-domain/v1/batches` and receive the same `500` and message 6. On the same proxy and with the same key, `POST https://litellm-domain/v1/files` followed by `POST https://litellm-domain/v1/batches` with the returned file ID succeeds with `200` **After a (hypothetical) fix: each unresolvable id returns 404 naming the object** 1. They send `GET https://litellm-domain/v1/batches/batch_68a1f2c9deadbeef` 2. The batch was purged and the id resolves to nothing 3. The response is `404` with `"No batch found with id 'batch_68a1f2c9deadbeef'."` and `"code": "batch_not_found"` 4. `POST https://litellm-domain/v1/batches/batch_68a1f2c9deadbeef/cancel` returns `404` with the same message 5. Submitting a batch with a mistyped `input_file_id` returns `404 "No such File object"` 6. The upload-then-create sequence still succeeds with `200` --- ### Proof the bug occurs **Version**: `litellm 1.94.3`, image digest `sha256:b7d979bac2a9e8fbb7d55272ef5f1f4a08ab365de8f78b1800834ca718d4c941` **Environment condition.** `OPENAI_API_KEY` and `OPENAI_API_BASE` must both be absent from the proxy environment. Two adjacent states produce different output: - `OPENAI_API_KEY` set to any value and `OPENAI_API_BASE` set to a reachable endpoint: `GET /v1/batches/{unknown_id}` returns 404 from that endpoint - `OPENAI_API_KEY=""` as an empty string: the same request returns 500 `Connection error.` Verified absent: ``` $ docker exec <proxy> sh -c 'env | grep -c "^OPENAI_API_KEY="; env | grep -c "^OPENAI_API_BASE="' 0 0 ``` **Config the proxy ran with** ```yaml model_list: - model_name: gpt-5-batch litellm_params: model: azure/gpt-5-batch-2025-08-07 api_base: os.environ/AZURE_API_BASE api_key: os.environ/AZURE_API_KEY general_settings: master_key: os.environ/LITELLM_MASTER_KEY database_url: os.environ/DATABASE_URL ``` **Commands and their full output** ``` $ curl -s -w '
HTTP %{http_code}
' http://localhost:4000/v1/batches/batch_does_not_exist_12345 \ -H "Authorization: Bearer $LITELLM_KEY" {"error":{"message":"The api_key client option must be set either by passing api_key to the client or by setting the OPENAI_API_KEY environment variable","type":"internal_server_error","param":"None","code":"500"}} HTTP 500 $ curl -s -w '
HTTP %{http_code}
' -X POST http://localhost:4000/v1/batches/batch_does_not_exist_12345/cancel \ -H "Authorization: Bearer $LITELLM_KEY" {"error":{"message":"The api_key client option must be set either by passing api_key to the client or by setting the OPENAI_API_KEY environment variable","type":"internal_server_error","param":"None","code":"500"}} HTTP 500 $ curl -s -w '
HTTP %{http_code}
' http://localhost:4000/v1/batches \ -H "Authorization: Bearer $LITELLM_KEY" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \ -d '{"input_file_id":"file-does-not-exist-12345","endpoint":"/v1/chat/completions","completion_window":"24h"}' {"error":{"message":"The api_key client option must be set either by passing api_key to the client or by setting the OPENAI_API_KEY environment variable","type":"internal_server_error","param":"None","code":"500"}} HTTP 500 ``` Same proxy, same key, same session, with a real uploaded file: ``` $ FILE_ID=$(curl -s http://localhost:4000/v1/files -H "Authorization: Bearer $LITELLM_KEY" \ -F purpose=batch -F 'target_model_names=gpt-5-batch' -F file=@batch_input.jsonl \ | python3 -c 'import json,sys; print(json.load(sys.stdin)["id"])') $ curl -s -w '
HTTP %{http_code}
' http://localhost:4000/v1/batches \ -H "Authorization: Bearer $LITELLM_KEY" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \ -d "{"input_file_id":"$FILE_ID","endpoint":"/v1/chat/completions","completion_window":"24h"}" {"id":"bGl0ZWxsbV9wcm94eTttb2RlbF9pZDo0ZDhhNWVmMGY2Y2M5OTZkMmEwYzlmYmEzYTMxMzQ5Mjg0OTYxNWNhM2E2YmJjNGRjOTcyMDQ0Mjg4MTBmMjk0O2xsbV9iYXRjaF9pZDpiYXRjaF8yMDI2MDgxNy0wNTU3LjAxOQ","completion_window":"24h", ...} HTTP 200 ``` ### list_batches The `:688` fallback was not reached on this configuration. Naming a provider returns 500 earlier: ``` $ curl -s -w '
HTTP %{http_code}
' 'http://localhost:4000/v1/batches?limit=5&provider=openai' \ -H "Authorization: Bearer $LITELLM_KEY" {"error":{"message":"Filtering by 'provider' is not supported when using managed batches.","type":"internal_server_error","param":"None","code":"500"}} HTTP 500 ``` ### What part of LiteLLM is this about? Proxy ### What LiteLLM version are you on ? v1.94.3

### Check for existing issues - [x] I have searched the existing issues and checked that my issue is not a duplicate. ### What happened? Same shadowing as #36086, on a different prefix. #36092 fixed `/openai_passthrough` and states "other provider prefixes keep today's behavior" — `/anthropic` is still affected on `main`. - `POST /anthropic/v1/files` is answered by LiteLLM's OpenAI files endpoint instead of being forwarded, and fails `422 {"loc":["body","purpose"],"msg":"Field required"}` - `purpose` is OpenAI-only. Anthropic's Files API has no such field, so the Anthropic SDK never sends one — `client.beta.files.upload({ file })` has no `purpose` param. The request cannot succeed - Adding `purpose` doesn't help: that path 500s on `files_settings is not set` - Regressed in v1.92.0 via [#30958](https://github.com/BerriAI/litellm/pull/30958/files#diff-cb47ff448a23857ca19cd50f8baa9aea47ee5cdefb475803fdc022449dc10d7eR15624), which moved `batches_router` and `openai_files_router` above the passthrough routers in `proxy_server.py`. Worked on v1.83.14-stable, where the order was reversed - `POST /anthropic/v1/files/` (trailing slash) is forwarded correctly, so it's route precedence, not the body Expected: `/anthropic/v1/files` forwards to `api.anthropic.com/v1/files` like every other path under `/anthropic/`. ### User Flow Before: a developer using the Anthropic SDK against the gateway cannot upload a document at all, so the model never sees their PDF. 1. They set base URL `https://litellm-domain/anthropic` and send `POST https://litellm-domain/anthropic/v1/files` with `file=@plan.pdf` — what `client.beta.files.upload({ file })` emits 2. They get `422 {"detail":[{"type":"missing","loc":["body","purpose"],"msg":"Field required"}]}`, no file id, and nothing in their Anthropic account 3. They add `purpose=user_data` and retry the same POST 4. They get `500 {"error":{"message":"files_settings is not set, set it on your config.yaml file."}}` 5. With no file id they cannot reference the document in `POST https://litellm-domain/anthropic/v1/messages`, so the answer ignores their PDF After: the same upload returns an Anthropic file id and the model reads the document. 1. They set base URL `https://litellm-domain/anthropic` and send the same `POST https://litellm-domain/anthropic/v1/files` with `file=@plan.pdf`, no extra fields 2. They get `200` with Anthropic's own file object — `{"type":"file","id":"file_011Ce8...","mime_type":"application/pdf"}` — visible in their account 3. They send `POST https://litellm-domain/anthropic/v1/messages` with a `document` block using that `file_id` 4. They get `200` and the reply quotes the PDF's contents ### Proof the bug occurs `config.yaml`: ```yaml model_list: - model_name: claude-haiku-4-5 litellm_params: model: anthropic/claude-haiku-4-5 api_key: os.environ/ANTHROPIC_API_KEY general_settings: master_key: sk-local-repro-master ``` Env: `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-invalid-key-for-local-repro`, `CONFIG_FILE_PATH=./config.yaml`, `LITELLM_MASTER_KEY=sk-local-repro-master` Version: `litellm==1.96.2`, run as `python -m uvicorn litellm.proxy.proxy_server:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 4000` The Anthropic key is invalid on purpose — it makes routing unambiguous for free. A request LiteLLM answers itself fails 422 on `purpose`; a request that is forwarded fails 401 at Anthropic. 1. What the SDK sends — intercepted, never forwarded: ``` $ curl -s -w "
HTTP %{http_code}
" -X POST http://127.0.0.1:4000/anthropic/v1/files \ -H "x-api-key: $MASTER_KEY" -H "anthropic-version: 2023-06-01" \ -H "anthropic-beta: files-api-2025-04-14" -F "file=@repro.pdf;type=application/pdf" {"detail":[{"type":"missing","loc":["body","purpose"],"msg":"Field required","input":null}]} HTTP 422 ``` 2. Trailing slash — forwarded, 401 from Anthropic as expected with an invalid key: ``` $ curl -s -w "
HTTP %{http_code}
" -X POST http://127.0.0.1:4000/anthropic/v1/files/ \ -H "x-api-key: $MASTER_KEY" -H "anthropic-version: 2023-06-01" \ -H "anthropic-beta: files-api-2025-04-14" -F "file=@repro.pdf;type=application/pdf" {"type":"error","error":{"type":"authentication_error","message":"API key is invalid."},"request_id":null} HTTP 401 ``` 3. Control — `/anthropic/v1/messages` forwards normally, same 401: ``` $ curl -s -X POST http://127.0.0.1:4000/anthropic/v1/messages \ -H "x-api-key: $MASTER_KEY" -H "anthropic-version: 2023-06-01" \ -H "content-type: application/json" \ -d '{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5","max_tokens":16,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":"hi"}]}' {"type":"error","error":{"type":"authentication_error","message":"API key is invalid."},"request_id":null} HTTP 401 ``` 2 and 3 prove the passthrough is wired correctly; 1 differs only in path shape. 4. With a valid Anthropic key on a v1.96.2 gateway (key and host redacted), the trailing-slash path completes the round trip: ``` POST /anthropic/v1/files/?beta=true {"type":"file","id":"file_011CeAPEhuywu41e5rH8h3Dp","size_bytes":401, "created_at":"2026-08-18T14:37:54.596000Z","filename":"repro.pdf", "mime_type":"application/pdf","downloadable":false} HTTP 200 POST /anthropic/v1/messages (document block referencing that file_id) {"content":[{"type":"text","text":"passthrough round trip ok"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn"} ``` "passthrough round trip ok" is the literal text in the uploaded PDF, so the model read the document. # Suggested fix - give `/anthropic` its own router mounted ahead of batches and files, as #36092 did for `/openai_passthrough` - or scope `/{provider}/v1/files` so it cannot shadow a registered passthrough prefix, which covers every provider whose native API has no `purpose` ### What part of LiteLLM is this about? Proxy ### What LiteLLM version are you on ? v1.96.2 ### Twitter / LinkedIn details _No response_

