## TLDR Problem this solves: - Internal Users get 401 listing their own teams - Admin UI key edit can't resolve the key's team How it solves it: - Self-scope an unfiltered team list to the caller - Only an explicit other user's `user_id` still 401s ## User Flow Before: an Internal User opening Virtual Keys cannot see any team, so editing a key's models fails 1. They log into the Admin UI as an Internal User and open https://litellm-domain/ui/?page=api-keys 2. The page asks for the team list with `GET https://litellm-domain/v2/team/list?page=1&page_size=100` and gets back 401 `{"error":"Only admin users can query all teams/other teams. Your user role=internal_user"}` 3. `GET https://litellm-domain/team/list` fails the same way, so the key's team never resolves and the models dropdown in the key edit view stays empty 4. Any other user's teams remain invisible to them, as intended After: the same user sees exactly the teams they belong to and can edit their key's models 1. They log into the Admin UI as an Internal User and open https://litellm-domain/ui/?page=api-keys 2. `GET https://litellm-domain/v2/team/list?page=1&page_size=100` returns 200 with `total: 1` and only the team they are a member of 3. `GET https://litellm-domain/team/list` returns that same single team, the key resolves its team, and the models dropdown populates 4. `GET https://litellm-domain/v2/team/list?user_id=<someone-else>` still returns 401, so another user's teams remain invisible to them ## Relevant issues ## Linear ticket Resolves LIT-5384 ## Pre-Submission checklist **Please complete all items before asking a LiteLLM maintainer to review your PR** - [x] I have added meaningful tests - [x] My PR passes all CI/CD checks (e.g., lint, format, unit tests) - [x] My PR's scope is as isolated as possible; it only solves 1 specific problem - [ ] I have received a Greptile **Confidence Score of at least 4/5** before requesting a maintainer review (Greptile reviews automatically once the PR is opened; 