## TLDR Problem this solves: - Vector store file reads returned 200 on provider 4xx - Callers saw an error body as a successful list - Only `get` skips `raise_for_status`, unlike post/delete How it solves it: - Raise on non-2xx in the six file read handlers - Errors now flow through the existing `_handle_error` mapping - Regression tests cover list, retrieve and content ## User Flow Before: a developer listing the files on a vector store gets HTTP 200 back even when the store is missing or the key is wrong, so their client parses an error object as a file list 1. They send GET https://litellm-domain/v1/vector_stores/vs_does_not_exist/files with their key 2. OpenAI answers 404 with `{"error": {"message": "No valid vector store found with id 'vs_does_not_exist'.", ...}}` 3. The gateway hands them HTTP 200 with that same error body 4. Their SDK treats the call as a success, so the failure surfaces later as a missing `data` field or an empty file list rather than an error 5. Same for GET /v1/vector_stores/{id}/files/{file_id} and its `/content` route After: the same request fails as a 404, so the client raises where the error happened 1. They send GET https://litellm-domain/v1/vector_stores/vs_does_not_exist/files with their key 2. OpenAI answers 404 with the same error body 3. The gateway now answers HTTP 404, and the provider's message is preserved in the response 4. Their SDK raises a not-found error on the call itself 5. Listing files on a store that does exist still returns HTTP 200 with the file list ## Relevant issues ## Linear ticket Resolves LIT-5604 ## Pre-Submission checklist - [x] I have added meaningful tests - [x] The handful of test files covering my change pass locally, e.g. `uv run pytest tests/test_litellm/<your_test_file>.py -v`. Leave the suites (`make test-unit-*`, `make test-unit`) to CI: it finishes in ~15 minutes where a laptop takes an hour or more - [x] My PR passes all required CI/CD checks (e.g., lint, schema.d.ts sync check, etc.) - [x] My P