## TLDR Problem this solves: - `/health/readiness` returns 503 during DB outage despite `allow_requests_on_db_unavailable: true` - K8s pulls every pod, so the fail-open setting never gets to run - Probe DB check is unbounded and can outlast kubelet timeout How it solves it: - Readiness keeps 200 during DB outage when the flag is on - Real DB state still reported in the body (`"db": "disconnected"`) - Flag off or unset keeps today's 503 behavior - DB round-trip on the probe path bounded to 2 seconds ## User Flow Before: a platform team enables `allow_requests_on_db_unavailable: true`, takes the DB down for maintenance, and every replica leaves rotation 1. They set `allow_requests_on_db_unavailable: true` under `general_settings` and roll the proxy 2. The DB goes offline for maintenance 3. GET https://litellm-domain/health/readiness returns `{"status":"healthy","db":"disconnected"}` with a 503, taking up to ~14s 4. Kubernetes marks all replicas NotReady, the service empties, and POST https://litellm-domain/v1/chat/completions and https://litellm-domain/ui/ come back 502 from the load balancer After: the same maintenance window keeps every replica serving 1. They set `allow_requests_on_db_unavailable: true` under `general_settings` and roll the proxy 2. The DB goes offline for maintenance 3. GET https://litellm-domain/health/readiness returns `{"status":"healthy","db":"disconnected"}` with a 200 in about 2s 4. Pods stay in rotation, POST https://litellm-domain/v1/chat/completions returns real completions, and https://litellm-domain/ui/ stays reachable 5. With the flag off or unset, a DB outage still fails readiness with a 503 as today ## Relevant issues Fixes #34934 ## Linear ticket ## Pre-Submission checklist **Please complete all items before asking a LiteLLM maintainer to review your PR** - [x] I have added meaningful tests - [x] The handful of test files covering my change pass locally, e.g. `uv run pytest tests/test_litellm/<your_test_file>.py -v`. Leave the suite