## TLDR Problem this solves: - Team admin delete restriction was UI-only, bypassable via API - No setting existed to stop team admins adding members - SCIM-provisioned team rosters could drift from the IdP How it solves it: - Adds `disable_team_admin_add_team_user` UI setting - Enforces both flags in `/team/member_add` and `/team/member_delete` - Proxy admins and org admins over the team stay unrestricted - Dashboard hides Add Member for a restricted team admin ## User Flow Before: an enterprise that provisions teams and members through SCIM cannot stop a team admin from changing their own team's roster, so the roster drifts from the IdP 1. The proxy admin opens https://litellm-domain/ui/?page=settings and turns on "Disable team admin delete team user", there is no equivalent add setting 2. A team admin opens https://litellm-domain/ui/?page=team_info&team_id=scim-team and sees no Delete icons, but "+ Add Member" is still there and works 3. The same team admin calls `POST https://litellm-domain/team/member_add` with `{"team_id": "scim-team", "member": {"user_id": "someone", "role": "user"}}` and gets `200` with the new member on the team 4. `POST https://litellm-domain/team/member_delete` with `{"team_id": "scim-team", "user_id": "someone"}` also returns `200` and removes the member, even though the setting is on 5. The next SCIM sync fights those manual edits, and any team admin can hand their team's models and budget to a user the IdP never provisioned After: the same restriction holds for both add and delete, from the UI and from the API 1. The proxy admin opens https://litellm-domain/ui/?page=settings and turns on "Disable team admin delete team user" plus the new "Disable team admin add team user" 2. A team admin opens https://litellm-domain/ui/?page=team_info&team_id=scim-team and sees neither Delete icons nor a "+ Add Member" button 3. The same team admin calls `POST https://litellm-domain/team/member_add` with the same body and gets `403` saying `Team admins are blocked from adding members to team_id=scim-team. Contact your proxy admin.` 4. `POST https://litellm-domain/team/member_delete` returns `403` saying `Team admins are blocked from removing members from team_id=scim-team.` and the roster is unchanged 5. The proxy admin, and an org admin over that team, still get `200` on both routes, so SCIM plus proxy-level administration stay the only ways the roster changes 6. A team admin can no longer grant a team's models and budget to a user the IdP never provisioned ## Relevant issues ## Linear ticket ## Pre-Submission checklist - [x] I have added meaningful tests - [x] The handful of test files covering my change pass locally, e.g. `uv run pytest tests/test_litellm/<your_test_file>.py -v`. Leave the suites (`make test-unit-*`, `make test-unit`) to CI: it finishes in ~15 minutes where a laptop takes an hour or more - [x] My PR passes all required CI/CD checks (e.g., lint, schema.d.ts sync check, etc.) - [x] My PR's scope is as isolated as possible; it only solves 1 specific problem - [ ] I have received a Greptile **Confidence Score of at least 4/5** before requesting a maintainer review (Greptile reviews automatically once the PR is opened; only comment `@greptileai` to re-request a review after pushing changes) ## Screenshots / Proof of Fix Run at 675a86b5b0 against a live proxy on `localhost:4000` with the dashboard dev server on `localhost:3000`, using a team-admin virtual key, an org-admin virtual key and the master key. Flags were toggled from Settings > UI with no proxy restart between steps ### Team admin blocked while the flags are on 1. In the dashboard, proxy admin turns on "Disable team admin add team user" and "Disable team admin delete team user", reload confirms `GET /get/ui_settings` reports both `true` 2. Team admin reloads their team page and the "+ Add Member" button is gone, rows and edit icons unaffected 3. Add: ``` $ curl -s -X POST -H "Authorization: Bearer $TEAM_ADMIN_KEY" -H "Content-Type: applica